            <ArticleTitle>Similarities in features of autism and asthma and a possible link to acetaminophen use.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.mehy.2009.08.033</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Autism and autism spectrum disorders are enigmatic conditions that have their origins in the interaction of genes and environmental factors. In this hypothesis, genes statistically associated with autism are emphasized to be important in inflammation and in innate immune pathways, including pathways for susceptibility to asthma. The role of acetaminophen (paracetamol) in an increased risk for asthma is described and a possible similar link to an increased risk for autism is suggested.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
